housandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T12:48:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T12:48:26Z","body":"You have violated our guidelines and I don't believe you, the other PR says it was authored by AI\r\n\r\nPlease do not try to contribute in this way again","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5293460769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5293562049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122404#issuecomment-5293562049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122404","id":5293562049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO4VYwQ","user":{"login":"Arcueid77","id":17421993,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDIxOTkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17421993?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77","html_url":"https://github.com/Arcueid77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arcueid77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T12:59:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T12:59:26Z","body":"For an issue that has existed for years, I find this response deeply disappointing.\n\nThe PR was closed and labeled as spam without any meaningful discussion of whether the patch is technically correct, whether it fixes the underlying issue, whether it introduces regressions, or whether the implementation approach itself is acceptable. Instead, the entire contribution seems to have been reduced to a judgment about AI involvement and the contributor's credibility.\n\nIs that really the standard expected from maintainers of a serious open-source project?\n\nHaving a policy around AI-assisted contributions is completely legitimate. Using that policy as a substitute for technical review is much harder to justify.\n\nIf the patch is wrong, explain what is wrong with it.\nIf it violates a specific contribution rule, point to the exact rule and explain what would need to change.\nIf the implementation is technically unacceptable, discuss the implementation.\n\nBut taking a proposed fix for a years-old issue, refusing to engage with the substance of the patch, labeling it `spam`, and then responding with “I don't believe you” and “Please do not try to contribute in this way again” does not look like code review. It looks like gatekeeping.\n\nAI involvement can absolutely be a reason to apply additional scrutiny. It should not be a one-click mechanism for avoiding scrutiny altogether.\n\nOpen source maintenance should ultimately be about correctness, maintainability, technical quality, provenance, and whether a contribution actually improves the project. If the code is bad, reject the code on technical grounds. If the process was violated, clearly identify the process violation. But dismissing the contribution primarily through an AI label, without addressing the actual fix, is not a healthy way to maintain a codebase.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5293562049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]